   474	**Lemma F_α [proved; [rec] Lemma F with √2 replaced by 2^α].** Let 0 < α < 1 and L_x := exp(Λ_α(x)) with
   475	Λ_α(x) := (log x)^α(max(1, log log x))^{1−α}. If F: [2, ∞) → [0, ∞) is nondecreasing and finite and, for x ≥ x₀,
   476	F(x) ≤ L_x^{p+ε(x)} + L_x^{δ+ε(x)}F(√(2x)) with ε(x) → 0, then F(x) ≤ L_x^{c+o(1)}, c := max(p, δ/(1 − 2^{−α})).
   477	*Proof.* Scaling: for y = √(2x), (log y)^α ≤ 2^{−α}(log x)^α + α2^{−α}(log 2)(log x)^{α−1} and log log y ≤ log log x, so
   478	Λ_α(y) ≤ 2^{−α}Λ_α(x) + o(1) and L_y^b ≤ e·L_x^{2^{−α}b} for x ≥ x₁(b). Then [rec]'s steps 2–5 verbatim with
   479	η′ := η(1 − 2^{−α})/4: in step 4 the second exponent is δ + η′ + (c + η)2^{−α} ≤ c + η2^{−α} + η′ = c + η − 3η′. ∎
