   517	## 11. The shared-rational-side multi-field trick
   518	
   519	**Design MF.** One rational side g (as before) and J_f independent algebraic sides (w_j, c_j), j ≤ J_f, giving
   520	F_j := F̂_{g,w_j} + G·R_{c_j}, all with F_j(g₀, g₁) = Nw_j and the common root m = g₀/g₁ mod N. (w_j = 1, i.e. design
   521	(a″_k), also works: Lemma W is not needed.) A prime ℓ is MF-descendable if some P ∈ 𝒫 ∩ Λ_ℓ(g) has Y_P = 1
   522	(rational, filtered) and F_j(P) ∈ 𝒮_B for some j.
   523	
   524	**Proposition MF [proved in outline: the moment part is proved; the multi-field post-processing is sketched].**
   525	Let γ_r := Pr_{g,ℓ}[∃P with Y_P = 1 and |G(P)| good]. If J_f ≥ (log N)^{C_g}/ρ_F, then
   526	  γ_MF := Pr_{g,(w_j,c_j),ℓ}[ℓ MF-descendable] ≥ γ_r/2,  and  γ_r ≥ (log N)^{−C}.
   527	*Proof.*
   528	- **Decoupling.** Condition on (g, ℓ) and on the event that some P has Y_P = 1 with t = |G(P)| good; let P₀ be the
   529	  first such P in a fixed order (a function of (g, ℓ)). By Lemma GM-U, for every w_j,
   530	  Pr_{c_j}[F_j(P₀) ∈ 𝒮_B] ≥ ρ_F/(log N)^{C_g} =: p₁ (its residue c_{P₀}w_j is a unit, [pp] Lemma `lem:coprime`).
